{
  "title": "Audit non-ingredient parentheticals preserved as notes",
  "description": "PR #500 intentionally broadened parenthetical preservation: \
if parenthetical content is not a valid alternate measurement, the parser now \
keeps it as an ingredient note. That avoids losing useful hints such as `(2 \
lemons)`, `(15-ounce)`, `(6-inch)`, and `(about 7 bones)`.\n\
\n\
The pipeline diff also shows some parentheticals that may be metadata rather \
than ingredient guidance. One curated example is `6 ounces vanilla wafers \
($1.43)`, which now parses as item `vanilla wafers` with note `$1.43`.\n\
\n\
This issue is to audit the new note population and decide whether any narrow \
classes should be filtered, normalized, or moved to a different field. Be \
conservative: package sizes, recipe fractions, yield hints, replacement hints, \
and `see note` references are usually useful to the cook and should not be \
discarded just because they are parenthetical.\n\
\n\
When changing behavior, add targeted parser tests and rerun `make pipeline` so \
reviewers can evaluate the real snapshot impact.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "task",
